\title{sciSpatialR: Spatial Harmonization and Covariate Extraction}
\description{
Provides tools for harmonizing spatial layers (masking,
resampling, aggregating) and extracting covariates at point
locations for Alberta-focused biodiversity and species
distribution modelling workflows.
}
\section{Reference Layers}{

Harmonization defaults to the Alberta provincial boundary and the
ABMI 1 km grid, both in NAD83 / Alberta 10-TM (Forest),
\code{EPSG:3400}.  Every function below that takes a reference grid or
boundary falls back to these, so layers harmonized with this
package share one CRS, extent, resolution, and origin unless a
caller opts out.
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ab_crs]{ab_crs()}} — default CRS, \code{"EPSG:3400"}
\item \code{\link[=ab_boundary]{ab_boundary()}} — Alberta provincial boundary (2020 revision)
\item \code{\link[=ab_grid]{ab_grid()}} — ABMI 1 km reference grid, 1234 x 695 cells
}
}

\section{Input and Validation}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=check_alignment]{check_alignment()}} — test CRS, extent, resolution, and origin
congruence against a reference grid
\item \code{\link[=harmonize_crs]{harmonize_crs()}} — transform points to raster CRS; warn if
raster reprojection would be implied
}
}

\section{Inspection}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=raster_stats]{raster_stats()}} — per-layer cell counts, missingness, and
value summaries
\item \code{\link[=plot_raster]{plot_raster()}} — quick-look ggplot2 map with a
quantile-stretched colour scale and boundary overlay
\item \code{\link[=plot_hist]{plot_hist()}} — histogram of cell values
\item \code{\link[=theme_science_map]{theme_science_map()}} — the ggplot2 theme those maps use
}
}

\section{Harmonization}{

\itemize{
